    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on 2026-07-27, **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.93) headline our offensive output. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Montero, providing a significant boost via wind-aided power potential and a strong platoon advantage. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** is locked in as a top-tier play; despite a rain risk, he faces a soft matchup against P\u00e9rez, where his raw power profile is enhanced by elite platoon splits. We are also capitalizing on the deteriorating form of Max Scherzer, as both **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Nasim Nunez** (62.09) see their efficiency scores elevated by the opportunity to exploit the aging veteran\u2019s 5.89 xERA.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (51.74) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Coby Mayo** maintains a solid base, he was squeezed out by the collective efficiency of our starters against the specific pitching profiles on the slate. **Curtis Mead** (55.09) ultimately holds the spot over him, as we are banking on his favorable BvP indicators and assumed #2 lineup slot to provide more immediate scoring opportunities than the bench alternatives. We are monitoring **Drake Baldwin** (61.71) and **Luis Robert Jr.** closely due to a 31% rain risk, which could shorten their involvement. Additionally, **Luis Lara** (49.07) is functioning near our floor; we are keeping him in the lineup primarily for his late-inning versatility, though he remains the first candidate to be subbed if defensive replacements are required later in the cycle.",
